{"arm": "X2-P", "compounds": 0, "compounds_kept": 0, "diagnoses": [{"cell": 7, "cost_per_unit": "About 95 us profiled per parse call (1.77 s cumulative / 18,683). Each fast scan sorts the trigger-char set and builds a tuple key before a C-level search. Each paragraph that holds a link also runs a per-character Python loop over the whole source to build a bracket map. It then parses every link d", "deal_round": 1, "doubling": "Roughly linear. Sections are independent, so doubling the document doubles parse calls, scans and bracket-map builds; wall time is about 2x. Nothing in the hot path is superlinear for this input.", "gap": "Two kinds of work exceed that minimum. First, per-scan re-derivation of the cached trigger regex: sorted() plus tuple compare plus two method calls, 55k times. Second, a whole-paragraph bracket map and link-range index built just to answer label_contains_link for labels that contain no '[' at all. T", "least_work": "One C-speed regex pass over each source's characters, plus a constant amount of Python work per emitted token. No full-source Python character loop is needed unless a link label actually contains a nested '['.", "library": "mistune", "run": 2, "unit_count": "18,683 InlineParser.parse calls, 55,819 _find_fast_text_end scans, 66,171 process_text calls, 4,031 bracket-map builds and 91,619 rendered tokens. About 700 sections are processed once.", "unit_of_work": "Inline parsing of one text source: a paragraph, list item, heading, table cell or link label. The fast text-end scan, scanner match and process_text run once per trigger character inside it."}], "experiment": "ideas-x2-round", "kept": 3, "lane_views": [{"lane": "obvious", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "24fad2a5"}, {"lane": "assume_less", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "24fad2a5"}, {"lane": "eliminate", "served_model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "view_sha": "24fad2a5"}, {"lane": "recombine", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "24fad2