{"arm": "X2-P", "compounds": 0, "compounds_kept": 0, "diagnoses": [{"cell": 10, "cost_per_unit": "About 1.6 us of self time per attempt (0.366 s / 233,596), and about 3.5 us cumulative including handleMatch and recursion. Each attempt also carries roughly 0.7 us of Registry.__getitem__ overhead. Most attempts find no match, so the cost is mostly Python wrapper work: method call, isinstance, the ", "deal_round": 1, "doubling": "The inline pattern work is linear: doubling the document roughly doubles the 233k attempts and their time. The abbr sibling lookup under the root grows quadratically in the number of top-level blocks, so its share roughly quadruples. The ancestor walks grow linearly in elements times nesting depth.", "gap": "Most of the about 2.3 s profiled time is interpreter overhead around misses. There are about 200k no-match attempts, each paying a full method call and setup. __build_ancestors re-walks the whole parent chain for every stacked element even though the stack entry already carries its parents. The abbr", "least_work": "One C-level regex scan per (segment, pattern), plus building and stashing an element only for real matches. Each element should get its ancestor tags once, in O(1) from its parent's list. The abbr pass should do one regex scan per text or tail, with insertion positions known in O(1).", "library": "markdown", "run": 2, "unit_count": "233,596 __applyPattern calls over 20,392 __handleInline calls, about 11.5 pattern attempts per text segment. They come with 237,430 Registry.__getitem__ calls, 16,524 ancestor-list rebuilds and 20,316 abbr iter_element visits.", "unit_of_work": "One inline-pattern attempt on one text segment: a call of InlineProcessor.__applyPattern for one (text, pattern) pair, driven by the while loop in __handleInline."}], "experiment": "ideas-x2-round", "kept": 1, "lane_views": [{"lane": "obvious", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "92287b51"}, {"lane": "name_the_problem", "served_model": "claude-