{"arm": "X2-P", "compounds": 0, "compounds_kept": 0, "diagnoses": [{"cell": 22, "cost_per_unit": "About 1.6 us of self time in __applyPattern (0.366 s / 233,596) plus about 0.7 us in Registry.__getitem__ (0.166 s / 237,430), plus the regex call. Together these are roughly a quarter of total profiled time (__applyPattern cumulative 35%).", "deal_round": 2, "doubling": "Linear. Doubling the document doubles the text nodes and therefore the attempts (about 16 patterns per node), so time roughly doubles. The per-node constant of ~11.5 Python-level attempts stays the same.", "gap": "Every pattern is attempted in Python for every string, even when the string holds none of that pattern's required characters. Plain tails, the text inside em/strong/code/link children and heading text mostly contain no '<', '&', '[', '\\\\' or backtick, so most of the ~233k attempts can never match.", "least_work": "Scan each text string once to find where markup characters occur, then do pattern work only for patterns whose required literal character (backtick, backslash, '[', '<', '&', '*', '_', newline) is present. That is O(total text length + number of matches).", "library": "markdown", "run": 2, "unit_count": "233,596 __applyPattern calls and 237,430 Registry.__getitem__ calls across 20,392 __handleInline calls. That is about 11.5 pattern attempts per text or tail string.", "unit_of_work": "One inline-pattern attempt: one (text string, inline pattern) pair tried by __handleInline through __applyPattern, which includes a Registry index lookup, a Python call, the ancestor check and a regex finditer."}], "experiment": "ideas-x2-round", "kept": 2, "lane_views": [{"lane": "obvious", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "92287b51"}, {"lane": "name_the_problem", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "92287b51"}, {"lane": "assume_less", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "92287b51"}, {"lane": "leap", "served_model": "claude-opus-5-5", "view_sha": "92287b51"}